  "$schema_note": "Canonical Bus A contract fixtures. Source of truth: internal-devops/contracts/bus-a/. Vendored copies are digest-checked; see README.md. Regenerate with scripts/generate-fixtures.mjs — do not hand-edit.",
  "contract_version": "1",
  "signature_header": "x-madfam-signature",
  "signature_format": "t=<unix-seconds>,v1=<hex hmac-sha256 over \"${t}.${raw_body}\">",
  "signing": {
    "secret": "whsec_bus_a_contract_fixture_not_a_real_secret",
    "fixed_timestamp": 1785196800,
    "note": "Synthetic test secret. Authenticates nothing, reaches no host. Consumers re-sign raw_body with this secret at test time to exercise the accept path, because a fixed past timestamp is correctly rejected by the replay window."
  },
  "required_fields": [
    "schema_version",
    "event_type",
    "event_id",
    "provider",
    "subscription_id",
    "organization_id",
    "amount_minor",
    "currency",
    "occurred_at"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "event_id is derived as `${event_type}:${source_event_id}` — never random. A random id turns a PSP retry into a duplicate entitlement grant.",
    "event_id is namespaced by event_type so one source event producing two lifecycle events cannot collide on a consumer idempotency key.",
    "raw_body is authoritative. Signatures cover exact bytes; parse-then-reserialize does not round-trip and will fail verification.",
    "An absent event_type means payment.succeeded — the pre-lifecycle emitter only ever sent that type.",
    "Unknown event_type must be ACKNOWLEDGED (2xx), not rejected. A 4xx makes the producer treat a forward-compatible event as permanently failed.",
    "amount_minor may legitimately be 0 on subscription.canceled. It must be > 0 on payment.refunded.",
    "An empty subscription_id or organization_id is a half-envelope: the producer skips it rather than dispatching, because consumers key entitlement on those and would ack-and-drop."
  ],
  "events": [
